Chosen message-id CHECK (same shape as r506/r508):
  CHECK (gmail_message_id ~ '^[a-f0-9]+$' OR (length(gmail_message_id) BETWEEN 8 AND 512 AND gmail_message_id !~ '[[:space:]]'))
Mailbox CHECK:
  CHECK (mailbox = ANY (ARRAY['pmbcontroller@gmail.com','pdc@pmgwa.com.au']))
pmbcontroller stays. Tightening to pdc@ only would reject the 26 stored rows.
New Outlook inserts write pdc@pmgwa.com.au. The legacy Gmail branch of
record_pdc_person_parts_complete_20260913 still requires pmbcontroller@gmail.com,
a hex id {10,40}, and gmail_receiving_provider.

Person recorder, new Outlook branch (management connection only):
  mailbox and to_address pdc@pmgwa.com.au
  verified_by microsoft_receiving_provider
  authentication_results starts mx.microsoft.com
  p_gmail_message_id length 8-512, no whitespace, and equals
    internet_message_id or outlook_message_id or microsoft_message_id
  SPF, DKIM or DMARC pass for the sender domain
  stock ^([0-9]{8}|IS[0-9]{8})$  (the table already allowed IS stocks; the function did not)
  body is exactly "parts complete [for] STOCK" or "STOCK parts complete"
  OR the body is only "Parts complete" and the subject contains that stock as its own token
  A longer sentence that merely contains the words is still refused.
