mark_pdc_parts_complete:
  Every board login still hits require_pdc_role('operator') (or the existing importer
  monitor denial). That is the "PDC role operator required" error.
  One added path: management_connection() is true (postgres, role none, no JWT, staging
  guard) AND the vehicle already has an active confirmation with mailbox pdc@pmgwa.com.au.
  Call record_pdc_person_parts_complete_20260913 first, then mark_pdc_parts_complete
  with the current vehicles.version.
  If parts_received is already true and the PARTS work item is not complete, the email
  path completes the work item. If both are already done, it returns ok true,
  code parts_already_received, changed false.
  A call with no pdc@ confirmation still raises PDC role operator required.
  Old mark md5 82d890802677a2ac93942d3f7b7bcd27. New mark md5 1a89be6cc2e0bac0e3be3112b30f379f.

Remaining gap (not changed here):
  import_actor() returns null. The authorization row for
  codex.pmb.importer.staging@pmb.local is not revoked, but that auth user is banned.
  recorded_by on the confirmation and updated_by / completed_by on the mark are nullable,
  so the write still lands, with a null actor. audit_pdc_event also stores auth.uid(),
  which is null on the management connection. This release does not unban that user
  and does not grant the importer role operator.

How Kajel should test, after this SQL is applied on staging only, as the management
connection (the same postgres session the hourly import already uses; no SET ROLE, no JWT).
Pass the Outlook internetMessageId in p_gmail_message_id. The parameter name is historical.

  select public.record_pdc_person_parts_complete_20260913(
    'IS60353006',
    '<the internetMessageId, including angle brackets if Outlook sent them>',
    '<received_at timestamptz>',
    'Vehicle To Service Purchase Order — Stock: IS60353006 P/O: GP10403460',
    'Parts complete',
    '<sha256 hex of the evidence, 64 chars>',
    jsonb_build_object(
      'mailbox','pdc@pmgwa.com.au',
      'to_address','pdc@pmgwa.com.au',
      'from_address','<the person@pmgwa.com.au on the message>',
      'header_from','pmgwa.com.au',
      'verified_by','microsoft_receiving_provider',
      'internet_message_id','<the same internetMessageId>',
      'authentication_results','mx.microsoft.com; spf=pass smtp.mailfrom=pmgwa.com.au; dkim=pass header.d=pmgwa.com.au; dmarc=pass header.from=pmgwa.com.au',
      'human_message','true',
      'unquoted_affirmative','true',
      'auto_submitted','no',
      'display_name','<the name on the message>'
    )
  );

The id must be 8 to 512 characters with no spaces. A Gmail hex id is not required.
header_from must be the sender's domain. The body passed in should be the unquoted
affirmation ("Parts complete"), not the whole MIME thread. The stock must be the
board stock, exactly IS60353006.

Then, same connection, using that vehicle's id and current version:

  select public.mark_pdc_parts_complete('<vehicle uuid>', <vehicles.version>);

A green box needs the confirmation row (parts_flags person_confirmed). The mark
completes the PARTS work item. It does not run unless the confirmation is already stored.

